{"kind":"assert","text":"E1: one boundary for what Explore must match. No more stops for it.\n\nRulings 34fb3c6d, d66ce570, 654ec50a, a870c343 and 1ffd7288 are one\nrule. Apply it to each further site without a new question.\n\nExplore matches the runtime, or answers unavailable, for two things:\n- the data that a rule reads from its Given: each value, each own key\n  in its order, and each descriptor.\n- each call of a method that an interface declares: its arguments,\n  its result and its throw.\n\nExplore gives no promise for the rest: the identity of an object or a\nfunction, a prototype, a constructor, function metadata, and a member\nof an implementation that no interface declares.\n\nA site of the first kind that does not match is a fault. Repair it.\nA site of the second kind needs no repair and no guard. List it in\nthe checkpoint. Stop for the planner only when a site fits neither\nkind, or when a shipped rule of Grow, Lending or Counter reads a site\nof the second kind.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}